! **Two iron atoms with antiparallel moments on a fully relativistic ultrasoft
! dataset**, which is the regime `MAGNETISM-NEXT.md` Q5 names as the largest
! validation gap in the noncollinear stack.
!
! Everything that only turns on when an augmented dataset carries several
! non-parallel moments has no external number of any kind: `add_becsum_so` on a
! textured `becsum`, `qq_so` inside an overlap whose two projectors sit on atoms
! whose spin frames differ, and the `fcoef` recombination that dresses both. A
! one-atom cell cannot reach any of them, because one atom is trivially parallel
! to itself, and every committed noncollinear reference here is either one atom
! (`fe-kind1-noncol.in`, `fe-noncolin-pbe-stress.in`) or norm-conserving
! (`h4-cycloid-90.in`). This cell and its canted partner `fe2-canted-soc.in` are
! the pair that reaches them, and the comparison is against `pw.x`.
!
! **The geometry is the conventional bcc cell with one atom displaced**, and the
! displacement is the point rather than an accident. Two atoms at the corner and
! the body centre are related by inversion, so the force on each is zero by
! symmetry and comparing forces would be comparing a residue, which is the trap
! `CLAUDE.md` records for the Born charges of a centrosymmetric crystal. Moving
! the second atom by 0.02 alat along x leaves a real force of order 1e-2
! Ry/bohr for the two codes to disagree about, and it is the same displacement
! in the canted cell, so the two magnetic arrangements are compared at one
! geometry.
!
! **The two atoms are two species pointing at one file**, because `angle1`,
! `angle2` and `starting_magnetization` are per species in `pw.x` and there is no
! other way to state a texture that both codes read the same way. A
! `STARTING_MOMENTS` card would be this code's own route and `pw.x` cannot read
! it, so the comparison would not be of the same input.
!
! The moments lie in the xy plane and point along +x and -x, so the state is a
! collinear antiferromagnet carried through the noncollinear machinery, which is
! what makes it the calibration of the pair: the canted cell is the one with a
! genuinely textured `becsum`, and a disagreement that is already present here is
! not about the texture.
!
! `nosym` because a vector density on a reduced k-set has to be symmetrised as an
! axial field on both sides, and the point of this cell is the augmentation terms
! rather than the symmetriser. `conv_thr` is 1e-11 rather than the 1e-8 an energy
! would want: a converged `dr2` bounds a moment two to four orders more weakly
! than it bounds an energy, measured three times in this project, and both the
! site moments and the forces are what is being compared.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 5.42, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 35.0, ecutrho = 280.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'marzari-vanderbilt', degauss = 0.02
    noncolin = .true.
    lspinorb = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.5
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    angle2(1) = 0.0
    angle1(2) = 90.0
    angle2(2) = 180.0
    nbnd = 40
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
    electron_maxstep = 200
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Fe1 55.845 Fe.rel-pbe-spn-rrkjus_psl.0.2.1.UPF
 Fe2 55.845 Fe.rel-pbe-spn-rrkjus_psl.0.2.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Fe1 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Fe2 0.52 0.50 0.50
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
